      "created_at": "2018-05-21T14:42:57Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-05-21T14:42:57Z",
      "body": "Encrypting the email address is not something the GDPR mandates. All the GDPR is about is that you as a business are upfront about what personal data you store, and for what purposes. Furthermore, upon user request you should hand over a dump of this data to the user and respect the user's request to be erased from your database. All of these are business processes that you can build on top of allauth....",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
