      "created_at": "2018-05-21T20:05:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-05-21T20:05:17Z",
      "body": "You are right, though it is a recommended procedure that personal information fields be protected even if someone obtains a copy of stored data as not to leak sensitive information by having those stored in plain text. It's a long shot that someone having hard data copy did not breach your codebase too (and could decrypt), but my ticket was more along those lines.\r\n\r\nClosing it is valid as is your explanation to why you closed it. Good to have such an answer about for others questioning what lengths to go to while complying.",
